WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.280
- Hey, what's up, everybody?

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.850
I'm back with Hallmark Christmas royalty,

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.370
Lacey Chabert, Candice Cameron Bure,

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.675
and Holly Robinson Peete, give it up.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.520
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.940
♪ This is ladies day ♪

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.657
This is not night, but yeah.

00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:15.540
(chuckles) Didn't think that through.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.470
It's no secret that people
love Hallmark Christmas movies.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.100
Some fans are so obsessed
they've watched all of them,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.320
and there are over 130.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.280
It's a lot of movies, just saying.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.650
It made us wonder, is it possible to spot

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.180
a fake Hallmark Christmas movie title?

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.070
Just saying.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:33.966
This is a game we're calling

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.580
Know your Hallmark Christmas movies?

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.552
Spot the fake and win a prize.

00:00:38.552 --> 00:00:41.379
♪ Know your Hallmark Christmas movies ♪

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:44.291
♪ Spot a fake and you could win ♪

00:00:44.291 --> 00:00:45.390
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.607
- [Lacey] Wow, it's impressive.

00:00:47.607 --> 00:00:48.536
- Oh, my God.

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:50.660
Do y'all have wine when
you think of these?

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:51.860
Like, is there wine involved?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.040
I love my team.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.873
(bells ringing)

00:00:54.873 --> 00:00:56.090
Jingle, jingle, girl.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.740
First, we need a contestant.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.059
Please welcome Jasmine
from Minneapolis, y'all.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:02.273
- Hi, hi, everyone.

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:04.900
- You look adorable.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.430
Say hi to Lacey, Candice, and Holly.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.263
- Hey, Jasmine.
- Hey, Jasmine!

00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:11.230
- Hi, Lacey. Hi, Candice. Hi, Holly.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.504
- Hi, Jasmine.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:15.030
- (laughs) Your voice got like

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.490
exponentially louder each time.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.600
It was Holly!

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.520
- I am so thrilled.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.700
- Oh, my God. No, I get it.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.860
If my sister were here, she would be like,

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.990
first of all, asking y'all
for all the swag in the world.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.810
But, Jasmine, exactly how big

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.469
of a Hallmark Christmas movie fan are you?

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:34.403
- I'm gonna make this clear.

00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:36.583
I am the hugest fan there is.

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:39.990
I love all the Hallmark movies.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.680
When COVID happened and
we were in quarantine,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.730
I was so happy when they decided

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.080
to play the Christmas movies on

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.970
the weekends to give us some joy.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.130
They just make you feel all good inside.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.800
And I make my husband watch them.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.930
I watch them with friends.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.040
A girlfriend and I won a contest last year

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.190
where we watched a bunch of movies.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.800
They just make me smile.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.070
- I love that, nothing wrong with that.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.480
Jasmine, are you ready to play the game?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.640
- I am.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.650
- All right, all right.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.960
Here's how it works,
Holly, Candice, and Lacey

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.450
will each read a list
of three movies titles

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.750
and their descriptions.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.970
One of those three will be fake.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.950
Jasmine has to guess which one.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.130
If she guesses correctly
two of three times,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.960
she'll get a very cool holiday vacation.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.720
And I'll try to help you out, Jasmine.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.000
Does that sound good?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.420
- Yes, thank you in advance, Kelly.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.700
- I don't know if I'll be
help, but I'm gonna try.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.360
All right, let's go,
Candice, you read first.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.950
- Okay, The Santa Incident.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.650
After his sleigh is shot down

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.970
while flying through military airspace,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.280
Santa is sought for questioning
by Homeland Security.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.824
Can Santa make them believe
in him before it's too late?

00:02:48.824 --> 00:02:53.080
Movie two, The Night Before
The Night Before Christmas.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.220
Santa crashes into the Fox family's house,

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.410
ends up with amnesia,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.160
and loses his magic sack of presents.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.870
The family must help Santa remember

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.620
who he is before Christmas is ruined.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.550
Movie C, Oh No, Ho Ho, Santa Quit?

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.077
When the world stops believing in him,

00:03:12.077 --> 00:03:14.270
Santa quits and heads to the beach

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.550
where he meets a girl whose Christmas wish

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.328
is to see her brother again.

00:03:18.328 --> 00:03:20.820
Santa must choose between pina coladas

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:24.050
and if one person
believing in him is enough.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.590
- Oh, my God.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.960
If that last one is a real movie,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.804
that will be what I'm watching tonight.

00:03:29.804 --> 00:03:32.020
(all laughing)

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.090
- I'm gonna say I agree.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:37.335
I'm going with C is not the real movie.

00:03:37.335 --> 00:03:38.510
- Just to remind you,

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.600
there's a holiday vacation
on the line, Jasmine.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.200
So, A, The Santa Incident.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.130
B, The Night Before The
Night Before Christmas.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.186
Or C, Oh No Ho Ho, Santa Quit?

00:03:49.186 --> 00:03:51.095
(all laughing)

00:03:51.095 --> 00:03:52.263
I hope it's that one.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.335
- Oh No Ho Ho, Santa Quit?

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:57.303
(bell dings)

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:02.303
- Okay, but can we please make this movie?

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:05.743
'Cause it sounds awesome (laughs).

00:04:05.743 --> 00:04:08.030
All right, wait. The
next one is from Holly.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:08.863
Go ahead.

00:04:08.863 --> 00:04:09.730
- Oh no, ho ho.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.000
Okay, here we go.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.720
So, okay, Jasmine, ready?

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.730
Movie A, It's Christmas, Carol.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.600
Heartless publishing executive Carol

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.360
is visited by three
ghosts of her former boss.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.010
Eve, Past Eve, Present
Eve and Future Eve, okay.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.000
They had to Eve for each ghost

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.310
due to budget costs in the afterlife.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.660
Okay, movie B, It's Christmas, Joy.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.580
You know, like the name?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.129
It's Christmas, comma Joy.

00:04:36.129 --> 00:04:39.360
Joy is a dental hygienist who needs

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.210
a Christmas boyfriend
to impress her parents.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.660
Desperate for a date,

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.010
Joy offers to drive Michael
home after his dental surgery.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.010
But instead gives him extra Vicodin, okay.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.710
And drives him to her parents' place.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.233
And movie C, Jasmine, It's Christmas, Eve.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.000
- Oh, with the eve, I gotcha.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.398
- It's Christmas, Eve.

00:05:01.398 --> 00:05:04.510
While stepping in as a
superintendent at her former school,

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.920
Eve is forced to cut the arts
program to balance the books.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.146
But then, she falls for a music teacher

00:05:10.146 --> 00:05:12.277
in fingerless gloves--

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.023
- Fingerless gloves?

00:05:16.023 --> 00:05:19.380
- Who helps her rediscover
the power of Christmas.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.340
Okay, Jasmine.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.522
- And the power of rock
and roll with those gloves.

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:25.970
I gotta be honest. Okay, wait.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.095
Which one is fake?

00:05:27.095 --> 00:05:30.431
I don't really still know
if I know what A is about.

00:05:30.431 --> 00:05:31.820
- I don't know.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.310
The Vicodin doesn't sound very Hallmark-y.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.960
So I'm gonna go with B,
It's Christmas, comma, Joy.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.530
- Yeah, I'm gonna say if that's real too,

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.997
you need to think about the times.

00:05:42.997 --> 00:05:46.500
(laughs) I don't think you
should be roofie-ing people

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.260
and taking them to your family.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.580
- Opioid Christmas is not--

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.310
- Yeah, I don't think it's gonna--

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.140
But let's make it for fun, guys.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.683
Is that the one? Is it B?

00:05:56.247 --> 00:05:57.398
(bell dings)

00:05:57.398 --> 00:05:58.481
Hey, you win!

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.090
(audience cheering)

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.172
We're actually sending you to

00:06:04.172 --> 00:06:07.640
one of the top Hallmark
Christmas locations,

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:08.850
the charming mountain town

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.510
of Park City, Utah, which I love.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.720
You will get four nights of modern

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.812
and luxurious accommodations
at Park City Peaks Hotel.

00:06:16.812 --> 00:06:20.860
And dine at the popular
Versante Hearth and Bar.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.480
It's gonna be awesome.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.580
Are you excited?

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.447
- I am excited, yay!

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.280
- Oh, my God. Love you so much.

